# Beat The Man V2 — Workflow Rules

These rules apply to every task, ticket, or request touching this repo.

## Workflow contract

Sam (and Claude, via mobile/desktop chat) are the product owners.
You are the developer. Follow this loop for every ticket, no exceptions:

1. INSPECT FIRST. Before proposing anything, actually investigate the
   relevant code, assets, or system you're about to build on. Check for
   existing similar scripts, fragile/fused structures, or unstated
   dependencies. Do not assume something is ready to build on - verify it.

2. POST A PLAN, DO NOT IMPLEMENT YET. Write your planned approach plus
   any real risks or open questions. Post it and STOP. If nothing needs
   flagging, explicitly say "no blockers found" rather than skipping
   this step.

3. WAIT FOR APPROVAL. Do not write or modify implementation code until
   you receive explicit approval. Writing a plan is not permission to
   proceed.

4. IF BLOCKED OR PLAN CHANGES MID-TASK, post an update and pause rather
   than silently continuing on a new assumption.

5. WHEN FINISHED, post a completion summary. Do not mark tickets as
   Done yourself - that's Sam's call.

Never skip steps 1-3, even for small, obvious, or "just a quick spike"
tickets.

## Reusability

Favor reusable, modular components. Check whether a reusable base
already exists (e.g. Character_Root hierarchy) before rebuilding.

## Source of truth

Ticket details live on Trello (Beat The Man V2 board). Always fetch
the actual card content rather than working from a paraphrase.